      "id": "sec-walk-it-out",
      "title": "WALK IT OUT",
      "order": 1,
      "questions": [
        {
          "id": "q-walk-it-out-1",
          "order": 1,
          "segments": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "SERMON REFLECTION GUIDE FOR THE WEEK OF JUNE 6TH - 7TH, 2026."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "q-walk-it-out-2",
          "order": 2,
          "segments": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Why do believers sometimes continue battling the same fear, temptation, or thought pattern even while the Holy Spirit is actively at work within them? Read these: "
            },
            {
              "type": "scripture",
              "displayText": "1 Cor 3:16",
              "reference": {
                "book": "1 Corinthians",
                "bookId": "1CO",
                "chapter": 3,
                "verseStart": 16
              }
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": " "
            },
            {
              "type": "scripture",
              "displayText": "Ephesians 4:23-24",
              "reference": {
                "book": "Ephesians",
                "bookId": "EPH",
                "chapter": 4,
                "verseStart": 23,
                "verseEnd": 24
              }
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": " "
            },
            {
              "type": "scripture",
              "displayText": "Rom 12:1-2",
              "reference": {
                "book": "Romans",
                "bookId": "ROM",
                "chapter": 12,
                "verseStart": 1,
                "verseEnd": 2
              }
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": " Dig deeper: What patterns in your life are shaping your battles- helping you or strengthening them? (Consider habits, relationships, repentance, and spiritual disciplines) What does victory actually look like biblically?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "q-walk-it-out-3",
          "order": 3,
          "segments": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "What battle are you most tempted to fight alone, and what keeps you from inviting God-or other people-into it? Dig deeper: Pride? Shame? Fear of vulnerability? Disappointment with unanswered prayers? What would it practically look like this week to stop fighting that battle alone?"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
